nd rested on \"MUST NOT round a value and continue\". A Go string carrying `\\xff`, or the WTF-8 lone-surrogate bytes `\\xed\\xa0\\x80`, is not valid text — but every Build entry hands it to `json.Marshal`, which substitutes U+FFFD and continues, and the omit-self identity is then sealed over the REWRITTEN bytes. Witnessed through your production entries: `BuildCaptureManifest` admits `source_identity.native_session_id = \"native\\xff\"` and seals `\"native�\"`, and `DecodeCaptureManifest` admits the sealed bytes; the same for `opaque_identity`; a lone surrogate seals as three U+FFFD; and — the part that makes this a correctness hole rather than a cosmetic one — `\"native\\xff\"` and `\"native\\xfe\"` seal BYTE-IDENTICAL manifests, so two distinct inputs collapse to one identity. `IdentityDigest(\"op\\xff\")` equals `IdentityDigest(\"op�\")`. The same rewrite happens at `BuildCanonicalSession` (title, actor name, actor model, extension strings), `BuildCanonicalEvent` (evidence native_type, reason codes), the capture item `exclusion_reason`, the boundary `source_generation` (`ParseGeneration(\"g\\xff\")` admits) and identity/item extension strings. Meanwhile every OTHER native-key admission refuses that byte with `native key is not valid UTF-8` — the arm your own rev4 corpus added and TRACEABILITY.md states as the sanitizer's bound, so these two entries launder a value past a gate the package documents as closed. Fix: a shared valid-UTF-8 text gate at EVERY Build-side string admission; sanitize `NativeSessionID` and `OpaqueIdentity` before `EncodeNativeIdentity` marshals them (or validate them inside the exported entry). Negatives at `BuildCaptureManifest` (source identity native and opaque), at `IdentityDigest` (opaque) and one per Build shape, each asserting that NO U+FFFD appears in the sealed bytes — assert the sealed bytes, not merely that the call refused. Ship one narrowing mutant and its harness row. Note the shape for your own checking: this is the same \"rewrite and continue\" class you closed for numbers, found one Section 1.6 rule away at text — when you close a rule of that class, sweep the sibling rules in the same paragraph.\n4|P3, all four small: (a) rebuild the producer evidence archive from a task-scoped directory so it carries no foreign artifacts and no `__pycache__`; (b) fix the `-0` / `+` / leading-zero sentence in TRACEABILITY.md; (c) add the build-side reason-code duplicate row and its harness row; (d) re-complete only the producer checklist rows.\n5|Procedure: your candidate is on base 2fc6d5074058ab7970c87982deac50b3e3f5fd91, which is current origin/main — do not refresh unless it actually moves; if it does, run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-24z2b3` and audit every path in `git diff --name-only 2fc6d50 <new base>` that also appears in your `git status`, keeping README/LOGBOOK edits additive on the NEW content. You are a FIRST leaf: do NOT touch internal/traceability (the final leaf TASK-260830-32ypr2 carries the registry bindings and the pin). Never commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept. Re-run the full configured validation suite once (command 5 is the race gate with `-timeout 25m` and can take 25-40 minutes under concurrent runs), update TASK-260830-24z2b3_results.md with a finding-by-finding table (finding -> change -> the test that fails without it -> evidence path), update the conformance matrix and the evidence archive (a real gzip archive, one raw log per plant with its subprocess exit, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1), re-complete the checklist, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-24z2b3 --role developer` so revision 5 is constructed, and exit promptly. Hand off no later than 2.5 hours in — the scope is one gate and four hygiene items.\n6|PARTIAL-ATTEMPT RECOVERY: if a previous attempt of this run died to a provider idle timeout, the Story worktree still carries its partial edits — start with `git -C .temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree status --short` and `git diff`, state what you inherited, and verify it against this brief instead of assuming it is correct.\n7|Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The same claude-opus-5 max reviewer contract applies to revision 5.","final_result":true}}}
