{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca33","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1a1-0fcd-7b72-b1bb-a101f0623221"},"sequence":884,"recorded_at":1780531400001763,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"96b9aaba-3389-40b6-a064-cffa078aa95e","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"96b9aaba-3389-40b6-a064-cffa078aa95e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"96b9aaba-3389-40b6-a064-cffa078aa95e"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b1a8-9f69-7282-8e11-b07ccb2d76d0"},"task_id":"01a0b1a8-9f69-7282-8e11-b07ccb2d76d0","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b1a8-9f69-7282-8e11-b07ccb2d76d0","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree/.temp/TASK-260830-24z2b3/rev5/TASK-260830-24z2b3_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-24z2b3 Results — implement-clone-bundle-and-canonical-session-types (rev4)\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review. Candidate left UNCOMMITTED in the Story\n4|worktree (`task-board/story/STORY-260830-1cyj0q`) on base `2fc6d50`\n5|(`origin/main` at handoff; refreshed from `888ae3d` via\n6|`task-board worktree refresh-candidate`); no commit on the Story\n7|branch. This is rework rev4 of review RUN-260917-62d051, which\n8|routed rev3 CHANGES REQUESTED with one P1, three P2, and seven P3\n9|findings (every rev2 finding verified fixed). Every finding is\n10|answered below with the change, the test that fails without it,\n11|and the evidence path.\n12|\n13|## Start-of-run recovery note\n14|\n15|When this run started, the worktree carried exactly the rev3\n16|candidate and nothing else: `M LOGBOOK.md`, `M README.md`,\n17|`?? internal/clonebundle/` (19 files + `testdata/mutant_harness.py`,\n18|matching the 21-path rev3 tree). No dead-attempt changes were\n19|present; verified with `git status` and `git diff` before the\n20|refresh, and every pre-existing change matches this brief's scope.\n21|\n22|The refresh replayed stale pre-v0.7.0 bytes into 30 trunk paths in\n23|the working tree (catalog/specdoc/specpin/traceability/`.task-board`\n24|reverted to v0.6.0 content, e.g. `catalog.Adopted = ReleaseV060`).\n25|Repaired by restoring trunk content (`git checkout HEAD -- .`) and\n26|re-applying the README section and LOGBOOK entry purely additively\n27|on top of the new trunk bytes; `task-board.config.json` ends\n28|byte-identical to HEAD. `git status` shows only candidate paths.\n29|No `internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings +\n30|re-pin). `SPEC.v0.7.0.md` §1.6 and §13.14.1 verified byte-identical\n31|to v0.6.0 (diff of the extracted sections, empty); authority cited\n32|as v0.7.0 with the same heading numbers.\n33|\n34|## Finding-by-finding table\n35|\n36|| Finding | Change | Test that fails without it | Evidence |\n37||---|---|---|---|\n38|| P1-c non-message payloads escape the number model + nested-duplicate rule at Build and Decode | `checkPayload` (`event.go`) runs `checkPayloadValues` — the shared value walker — over the whole payload for every kind, then decodes with `UseNumber` and converts to exact int64 (`convertPayloadNumbers`); host float64 never appears, so sealed bytes cannot round or collapse. Shape faults report as payload faults (`errPayloadShape`, `decode.go`) | `TestCanonicalEventPayloadValueModel`: build negatives (1.5, 2^53, 2^53+1, -(2^53), 2^60, 1e2, nested/array-nested duplicates across usage/tool_call/opaque_event/error), decode negatives, resealed-decode negatives, sealed-bytes exactness (2^53-1, -(2^53-1), nested), message regression, 300-deep bound | `pkg-test.log`, `mutants/run1/N-payload-number.log`, `mutants/run2/N-payload-number.log` |\n39|| P2-α extension-value gate measured at 2 of 17 sites | `TestExtensionValueModelAtEverySite`: one value-fault row per admission site (16 decode sites + shared build helper), all injecting `{\"com.example.n\":1.5}`; the two payload-level rows pin the site detail (`message payload extensions`, `content block[0] extensions`) because the whole-payload gate also refuses there | Each of the 17 `N-ext-values-*` harness rows kills exactly its row | `pkg-test.log`, `mutants/run1/N-ext-values-*.log`, `mutants/run2/N-ext-values-*.log` (17 logs per run) |\n40|| P2-β decode equal-key duplicate raw entry unmeasured | Decode `duplicate entries` row added to `TestRawManifestRefusals/decode` (code already refused) | `TestRawManifestRefusals/decode/duplicate_entries` | `mutants/run1/N-raw-order-decode.log`, `mutants/run2/N-raw-order-decode.log` |\n41|| P2-γ duplicate plan keys defeat one-per-plan-candidate | `checkPlanItemMatch` (`capturebuild.go`) refuses duplicate plan keys outright | `TestCaptureManifestRefusals/build_plan_match` (plan `[a,a,token]` case, the P5c vector) | `mutants/run1/N-plan-keys-dup.log`, `mutants/run2/N-plan-keys-dup.log` |\n42|| P3-a′ content `null` passes the XOR | XOR is a non-null test (`event.go`); null content and null descriptor both refuse as not-exclusive | `block null content`, `block null descriptor` rows in `TestCanonicalEventRefusals/build_envelope` | `pkg-test.log`, `mutants/run1/N-block-content-null.log`, `mutants/run2/N-block-content-null.log` |\n43|| P3-b′ refusal detail misreports value faults | `captureitem.go`, `session.go`, `event.go` block site use `%s` with the fault like the other 13 sites | `TestExtensionValueModelAtEverySite/capture_item`, `/actor`, `/content_block` assert the fault text (`safe-integer` / site detail) | `pkg-test.log` |\n44|| P3-c′ input_blocked arm unmeasured | `closed_store input_blocked false` row in `TestBoundaryRefusals/decode stable proof` | same row | `mutants/run1/N-proof-input-blocked.log`, `mutants/run2/N-proof-input-blocked.log` |\n45|| P3-c′ -(2^53) arm unmeasured | `decode negative 2^53` row in `TestRawManifestRefusals/extension_values` | same row | `mutants/run1/N-ax-number-negative-edge.log`, `mutants/run2/N-ax-number-negative-edge.log` |\n46|| P3-c′ Zp arm unmeasured | U+2029 row in the `TestIdentityRefusals/sanitizer` corpus | same corpus | `mutants/run1/N-sanitizer-zp.log`, `mutants/run2/N-sanitizer-zp.log` |\n47|| P3-c′ payload top-level duplicate unmeasured | `payload top-level duplicate` row in `TestCanonicalEventRefusals/build_envelope` (pins `duplicate member`) | same row | `mutants/run1/N-payload-top-dup.log`, `mutants/run2/N-payload-top-dup.log` |\n48|| P3-c′ decode external-null-parent unmeasured | `external null parent` row in `TestCanonicalSessionRefusals/decode` | same row | `mutants/run1/N-decode-external-null-parent.log`, `mutants/run2/N-decode-external-null-parent.log` |\n49|| P3-d′ `EncodeNativeIdentity` rounds unsafe extensions | The exported entry validates extensions via `encodeExtensions` (`identity.go`); the \"never admits what decoding refused\" sentence is now true. The bad-extensions `IdentityDigest` row now fires at encode (`reverse-DNS`) | `TestEncodeNativeIdentityRefusals` (2^60 refuses, bad key refuses, valid round-trips) | `pkg-test.log`, `mutants/run1/N-encode-identity-extensions.log`, `mutants/run2/N-encode-identity-extensions.log` |\n50|| P3-e′ `N-main-count` note over-claims | Split into per-site `N-main-count-build` + `N-main-count-decode`, each with its site's killer | `TestCanonicalSessionRefusals/build_actors/two_mains`, `/decode/two_mains` | both per-plant logs per run |\n51|| P3-f′ dead code | Removed `sourceBasisObject`, `digestOrEmpty`, `digestOrEmptyDigest` (`boundary.go`; no callers) | `go vet`, suite | `cmd03.log`, `pkg-test.log` |\n52|| P3-g′ census arms | Rows added: version≠1.0.0 at capture/session/event decode; entries/items/actors/raw_refs not-an-array; 65536 entries/items/raw_refs, 1024 actors, 128 reason-codes maxima; build byte_count/ordinal/offset/length uint53 overflows; invalid-UTF-8 sanitizer row. Stated as defense-in-depth in TRACEABILITY.md: descriptor member-parse arms (owner enforces first), total_bytes overflow (unreachable with real payloads), C1-beyond-U+0085 / fraction-subsumption / exact depth edge (informational) | the named rows in `TestRawManifestRefusals`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals`, `TestCanonicalSessionRefusals`, `TestCanonicalEventRefusals`, `TestIdentityRefusals/sanitizer` | `pkg-test.log` |\n53|\n54|Also: `doc.go` and `TRACEABILITY.md` authority moved to\n55|`SPEC.v0.7.0.md`; the value-model bound restated (fact registry\n56|stays sibling scope, the §1.6 value model is enforced here for\n57|every payload member); the `C-doc-comment` control anchor follows\n58|the authority line.\n59|\n60|## AC coverage: 18 of 18 rows driven\n61|\n62|See `TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md` (rev4): every row\n63|names its production call site and driving test. Strengthened rows\n64|since rev3: 4 (Zp + invalid-UTF-8 sanitizer rows), 6 (decode item\n65|rules + version/not-array/maxima rows), 7 (XOR null arms), 10\n66|(duplicate plan keys), 12/13 (per-site extension rows,\n67|input_blocked), 15 (encode-time extension validation), 16/17\n68|(decode actor/event rows + payload value model), 18 (unchanged,\n69|still linked).\n70|\n71|## Validation reran in rev4 (this run, final tree)\n72|\n73|- Commands 1-3 (`gofmt` check, `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`):\n74|  PASS (`cmd01.log`, `cmd02.log`, `cmd03.log`)\n75|- Command 4 (`go test ./... -count=1 -v`): PASS, 16950 passes,\n76|  no FAIL (`cmd04.log`)\n77|- Command 5 (`go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m`): PASS,\n78|  38 packages ok, zero `DATA RACE` lines\n79|  (`ok internal/sessquery 390.722s`, `ok internal/clonebundle\n80|  4.369s`) (`cmd05.log`)\n81|- Command 6 (`go test ./... -cover -count=1`): PASS, 38 packages\n82|  ok, clonebundle 86.8% statements (`cmd06.log`)\n83|- Commands 7-20 (fuzz smokes, 14 targets): PASS\n84|  (`cmd07.log` … `cmd20.log`)\n85|- Commands 21-22 (`tracecheck`, `cataloggen -adopted -check`):\n86|  PASS (`cmd21.log`, `cmd22.log`)\n87|- Commands 23-24 (`GOOS=linux/windows` builds): PASS\n88|  (`cmd23.log`, `cmd24.log`)\n89|- Commands 25-27 (JSON validation, `task-board validate`,\n90|  `git diff --check`): PASS (`cmd25.log`, `cmd26.log`, `cmd27.log`)\n91|- Package suite: PASS (`pkg-test.log`), 86.8% statements\n92|  (`pkg-cover.log`); package race PASS (`pkg-race.log`)\n93|- Mutant harness: 64 KILLED + 1 SURVIVED control, full battery run\n94|  twice with per-plant raw logs (`mutants/run1/*.log`,\n95|  `mutants/run2/*.log`, `mutants-run1.log`, `mutants-run2.log`),\n96|  `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`\n97|- No `internal/traceability` edit; candidate paths only in\n98|  `git status` (plus the untracked package dir, same as rev3)\n99|- Reviewer-vector confirmation: the rev3 probe battery\n100|  (`zz_rev3_probe_test.go.txt`) executed once against the new tree\n101|  in a throwaway run (file removed afterwards; `rev3-probes.log`):\n102|  all 28 N1 build vectors and all 7 N2 resealed-decode vectors\n103|  REFUSE; P5c/P7d/P7e/P20c refuse; P2u now refuses (intended P3-d\n104|  behavior change); safe edges and valid shapes still admit\n105|\n106|## Bounds for siblings (not waived)\n107|\n108|- Per-kind event payload fact registries: which facts a kind may\n109|  carry (normalization sibling). The §1.6 value model on every\n110|  payload member is enforced here, not bounded away.\n111|- `maximal_safe` projection planning past\n112|  `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete` (projection sibling).\n113|- Target-branch (G2) admission past `RefuseUnstableForTarget`.\n114|- Section 7.8 operation wiring (stays `sessadapter`).\n115|- `-0`/`+n`/leading-zero literals admit by\n116|  `canonicaljson.validateAXNumbers` parity (stated, not waived).\n117|- `internal/traceability` bindings + re-pin (FINAL leaf).\n118|\n119|## Attachments\n120|\n121|- `TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md` (rev4)\n122|- `TASK-260830-24z2b3_producer-evidence.tar.gz` (rev4 logs:\n123|  27-command suite, package suite, 2x64+1 mutant battery with\n124|  per-plant logs, file manifest)","final_result":true}}}
