{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d057","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1a1-0fcd-7b72-b1bb-a101f0623221"},"sequence":1670,"recorded_at":1780531400003335,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"96b9aaba-3389-40b6-a064-cffa078aa95e","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"96b9aaba-3389-40b6-a064-cffa078aa95e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"96b9aaba-3389-40b6-a064-cffa078aa95e"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b1bc-f9ef-7143-803a-e72bca27b4e6"},"task_id":"01a0b1bc-f9ef-7143-803a-e72bca27b4e6","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b1bc-f9ef-7143-803a-e72bca27b4e6","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-34-1\",\n  \"command\": \"head -n 40 LOGBOOK.md; echo \\\"===DIFF===\\\"; git diff LOGBOOK.md | head -n 30\",\n  \"description\": \"Check LOGBOOK newest-first format\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260830-24z2b3 — clone bundle + canonical session/event types (first leaf)\\n\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/clonebundle` implements the Section 13.14.1 capture contracts over the landed owners — Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0, Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 (Capture Items, Source Basis, Capture Boundary, core-derived `raw_complete`), Canonical Session 1.0.0 + Actors, Canonical Event 1.0.0 (Source Evidence, raw refs, content blocks), NativeIdentity/WorkspaceBinding, immutable generations — plus Section 10.2 descriptor agreement and no-replace install via `localstore`. Every Build entry is byte-identical for identical inputs; every Decode entry enforces the closed shape. Row-21 exclusion allowlist (`hosttrust` matchers) enforced at raw-entry and capture-item construction with per-class negatives.\\n- OWNERSHIP: `canonicaljson` keeps its `rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape` rows (that table's census pins every row); this package is the validating owner and reuses `Canonicalize` (byte transform), `CalculateObjectIdentity` plus local claim comparisons (blobs; never the attesting `VerifyObjectIdentity` entry — only the test fixture calls it — per the provhost no-attestation bound), `sessadapter.DecodeTuple`, the `environ` scalar gate set via delegating wrappers, `scalar`, `hosttrust`, and `localstore.PutBlob`. No `internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings + re-pin); clause map in `internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n- EVIDENCE: package suite green (86.8% statements), 64 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, one raw log per plant with subprocess exit, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`); `TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent` + `TestInstallRawBlobRefusals` prove the localstore delegation (double install agrees; forged claim, short/long/tampered bytes refuse); durability itself is the landed localstore discipline (purity bound for this package: no second write path). README package section added with test commands and no capability claim.\\n- REV3 (rework of review RUN-260917-c05bc8): P1-a descriptor identity linked to the entry at build + evidence verification; P1-b AX number model + nested-duplicate refusal on extension values at build + decode; P2-f/P2-a environ gate adoption with the character string measure; P2-b/P2-c decode-side negatives for every surviving row + verifier/install negatives with per-plant logs; P2-d duplicate raw keys refused; P2-e identity re-decode before hashing; P3-b content XOR enforced; P3-c one-per-plan-candidate refused at build; P3-a sanitizer hardened with the exact bound stated; P3-d/P3-e harness rows fixed; P3-f/g/h hygiene. Finding-by-finding table in `TASK-260830-24z2b3_results.md`.\\n- REV4 (rework of review RUN-260917-62d051; base refreshed 888ae3d→2fc6d50, authority now SPEC.v0.7.0 with byte-identical pinned sections): P1-c payload value model enforced for every event kind at build + decode with exact-int64 sealing (sealed bytes never round/collapse); P2-α one extension value-fault row per admission site (17 rows + 17 narrowing plants); P2-β decode duplicate-entry row; P2-γ duplicate plan keys refused; P3 null-content XOR, refusal-detail fixes, input_blocked/-(2^53)/U+2029/payload-top-dup/external-null-parent rows, EncodeNativeIdentity validation, N-main-count split, dead code removed, census version/not-array/maxima/overflow rows with the remainder stated as defense-in-depth. Finding-by-finding table in `TASK-260830-24z2b3_results.md`.\\n- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): per-kind event payload fact registries past the envelope (which facts a kind may carry; the §1.6 value model on every payload member is enforced here); `maximal_safe` planning past the refusal gate; G2 admission past `RefuseUnstableForTarget`; Section 7.8 operation wiring (stays `sessadapter`). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n- AC: 18 of 18 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `TASK-260830-24z2b3_conformance-matrix.md`).\\n\\n### TASK-260917-10k118: reconstructed the reviewed v0.7.0 adoption on trunk 7efe385 (STORY-260916-3uqbwq unlandable, accepted CRs frozen)\\n- METHOD: true pin delta is `git diff e4e3e88 9cb5dd4` (10 files) — the exported 238-file patch diffs unrelated tips and would revert five landed stories, so it was used as transport only; rev3 candidate bytes applied (15 modified + 3 new) with the 5 trunk-merged files copied verbatim after diff-review (no trunk test lost, `task-board.config.json` untouched). All 19 machine-applied files `cmp`-identical to the rev3 bytes; ownership sha256 `2548870d…8a5070`, projection digest `c4cd46bf…53473f6` recomputed two independent ways.\\n- RE-VERIFIED (this session, fresh clone + production helpers): tag `d4abe46f…795b3` Good, peeled `32b3f2ba…321834`, SPEC blob `c4903e60…1ddd86` 1185291 bytes sha256 `c6b2fe64…89ddcf` byte-identical to `SPEC.v0.7.0.md`; lock 64/64 rows order- and set-identical to the §1.5 table (1 known order normalization); 65/65 bindings + 132/132 cases carried with 3 reviewed additions each; all 49 discharged clauses re-measured (uniform +20/+79/+185/+281/+392, excerpts verbatim); rev3 prose says \\\"48 carried clause lines\\\" in two places — measured 49, matching the 49/569 numerator; artifact is right, prose miscounted.\\n- FINDING F1: the reviewed v0.7.0 source normative-section group keeps production `VerifyV060` while its cases moved to the v0.7.0 pair; the v0.5.0→v0.6.0 precedent moved `Verify`→`VerifyV060`, so the pattern says `VerifyV070`. Green because the gate checks declaration existence only. Reviewed bytes are not rewritten in a reconstruction; the new re-derivation test pins the carried reference literally with the rationale.\\n- NEW TESTS (this Story's scope): `TestV070RegistryRederivesFromTrunkV060Registry` (carry completeness, clause re-measurement via production inventory+quote, no self-minted claims) and `TestREADMEMeasuredCoverageMatchesTracecheckReport` (fenced line byte-equal to tool output, 8 headline prose figures re-derived). Narrowing mutants per test + token-preserving README plant with full behavioral suites; harmless controls SURVIVED. Full 27-command suite green on the exact tree.\\n- FIGURES: contracts=64, acceptance cases=135, bindings=68, clauses 49/569. No launch-plan/stdin/caller_launch_plan/environment_drift/curator-run runtime claim.\\n- STATUS: implemented, tests green, ready for review; work left UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for the handoff snapshot.\\n\\n### TASK-260916-n9r71p: bound v0.7.0 launch-plan catalog row and curator story owners\\n- AUTHORITY: catalogue generation, Current, CI roots and traceability consume the adopted v0.7.0 lock/document/inventory; four release projections preserve V060/V050/V043 history. Metadata digest `c4094101…50274a35`; ownership digest `c4cd46bf…53473f6`. Localstore stays on explicit CurrentV050. Validation command 22 is the release-agnostic `-adopted` gate, which resolves to the v0.7.0 metadata/lock pair on this tree.\\n- DELTA: +Launch Plan request `urn:ax:schema:launch-plan-request` 1.0.0 (64th row, census-only, no catalog family); provider families carry the 2.1.0/3.1.0 minors (SPEC 7.5 adds members not operations; consumers range over names); session-record 3.1.0, error 1.4.0/1.5.0 and manifest/probe 1.1.0 stay census-only (carrying 3.1.0 panics canonicaljson init — no Go shape validator yet — same init-panic rationale as error 1.4.0). +3 section bindings (13.1, 13.10, 14.1), +1 fixture (`pin:ax-launch-plan-request-v1`), gaps updated for 5.1/7.3/7.4/7.5/appendix-d with story owners; 48 carried clause lines re-measured against SPEC.v0.7.0.md (uniform +20/+79/+185/+281/+392 shifts, every excerpt verbatim, no ID shifts).\\n- OWNERS: all 7 launch-plan clause areas name implementing EPIC-260916-18uelk stories with unevidenced coverage — 3fjjtn parsing/refusals (14.1, 13.1, contract), 2q85nu record embedding (5.1), 1kp1lx stdin/replay (7.5), 1ea7od plugin capability (7.3/7.4), 3aukw3 drift (13.10), 3ustb3 naming (13.1 split), vucwn0 vectors (fixture, appendix-d split). The source-derived AdoptedSections test requires 6/6 plus 2 split attributions and refuses each through VerifyAssignedSections.\\n- HISTORY: registry re-derived from the trunk-final v0.6.0 registry, carrying the five landed stories' 31 acceptance cases and 9 section bindings (2.2, 2.4, 5.3/5.4/5.5, 6.6, 7.7, 8, 10.6, 11.10.1–4, 13.12/13.13, 16.1) with re-measured clause lines; v0.6.0/v0.5.0 locks, registries, readers and historical tests byte-untouched versus trunk; the v0.7.0 inventory is identifier-equal to v0.6.0 (170 ids, same digest), so legacy verification derives both historical registries from the adopted lock. P3 closed: pin.go/specdoc.go consumer comments now true in the present tense; section:11.10.5 carried as a Disclosure owner (source evidence only, no implementation claim).\\n- FIGURES: contracts=64, normative section keys=36, acceptance cases=135, fixtures=33, historical contracts=55; bindings=68 (full=2, partial=6, sliver=4, unevidenced=52, unmeasured=4), unowned=7, discharged clauses=49/569. No launch-plan/stdin/caller_launch_plan/environment_drift/curator-run runtime claim anywhere.\\n- STATUS: implemented, tests green, ready for review; work left UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for the handoff snapshot.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go` + `hostile_carrier_test.go` re-derive all seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` entries with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, and execute the AC-HOST-001 rows: real OpenSSH loopback carrier (unprivileged `sshd`, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation/enrollment lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, and the v4 loader gate. Test-only leaf; no production file changed. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).\\n- F1: when the SERVER refuses mid-handshake, production `Dial` stably reports `transport_failure` (alert/close rendezvous; TLS 1.3 lets the client finish first) while `Serve` deterministically reports `authentication_failed`; only the initiator's OWN verification failure surfaces as `authentication_failed` on `Dial`. Tests pin both sides; the rendezvous resolves at the hello bound.\\n- F2 (MEASURED BOUND): an idle stream with zero traffic does NOT self-close within one second of revocation — `serveLoop` carries no background watchdog. The next dispatch fences in milliseconds and `WatchGeneration` reports the commit; recorded as a stated bound with log evidence, not a pass. Tailscale SSH and non-host lanes likewise bounded.\\n- F3: `os/exec.Cmd.Wait` called twice hangs the second caller forever — test cleanup consumes one `Wait` channel. The 8 MiB line cap is enforced twice (framing + decode), so the oversize mutant weakens both layers in one multi-file probe (harness extended for `(file, old, new)` triples). The Structured Error schema URN is `urn:ax:schema:error`; a drift vector with the wrong URN passed for the wrong reason until the mutant survived and exposed it.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 9 new narrowing probes, all killed by named `TestHostile*` vectors (same-family ALPN, dual-layer oversize, client rebind, rpc-contracts, error-version drift, truncated-dispatch ignore, snapshot integrity, correlation, static nonce); pre-existing 26 probes re-run green (neutral passed, client-cache documented SURVIVED). Per-plant logs/tables in the outcome tar.\\n- TRACEABILITY: `AC-HOST-001` registered over 20 suite tests; new `unevidenced` bindings for 11.10.1–11.10.4 + 16.1 with honest gaps (executed lanes vs stated bounds); 6.6/11.10 gaps refreshed; 11.10.5 stays unowned by design (no policy reader); digest re-pinned `e327bb08...`; report 102 cases / 61 bindings / 8 unowned / 17/487 clauses; README figures + tracecheck pins updated.\\n===DIFF===\\ndiff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex 8022478..a86a9ef 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -5,6 +5,16 @@\\n \\n ## 2026-09-17\\n \\n+### TASK-260830-24z2b3 — clone bundle + canonical session/event types (first leaf)\\n+\\n+- DELIVERED: `internal/clonebundle` implements the Section 13.14.1 capture contracts over the landed owners — Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0, Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 (Capture Items, Source Basis, Capture Boundary, core-derived `raw_complete`), Canonical Session 1.0.0 + Actors, Canonical Event 1.0.0 (Source Evidence, raw refs, content blocks), NativeIdentity/WorkspaceBinding, immutable generations — plus Section 10.2 descriptor agreement and no-replace install via `localstore`. Every Build entry is byte-identical for identical 