{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d05b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1a1-0fcd-7b72-b1bb-a101f0623221"},"sequence":1672,"recorded_at":1780531400003339,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"96b9aaba-3389-40b6-a064-cffa078aa95e","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"96b9aaba-3389-40b6-a064-cffa078aa95e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"96b9aaba-3389-40b6-a064-cffa078aa95e"},"call_id":"call_01a0b1bcf41d76299611007d7c07226a","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-34-1\",\n  \"command\": \"head -n 40 LOGBOOK.md; echo \\\"===DIFF===\\\"; git diff LOGBOOK.md | head -n 30\",\n  \"description\": \"Check LOGBOOK newest-first format\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260830-24z2b3 — clone bundle + canonical session/event types (first leaf)\\n\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/clonebundle` implements the Section 13.14.1 capture contracts over the landed owners — Clone Raw Object Manifest 1.0.0, Clone Capture Manifest 1.0.0 (Capture Items, Source Basis, Capture Boundary, core-derived `raw_complete`), Canonical Session 1.0.0 + Actors, Canonical Event 1.0.0 (Source Evidence, raw refs, content blocks), NativeIdentity/WorkspaceBinding, immutable generations — plus Section 10.2 descriptor agreement and no-replace install via `localstore`. Every Build entry is byte-identical for identical inputs; every Decode entry enforces the closed shape. Row-21 exclusion allowlist (`hosttrust` matchers) enforced at raw-entry and capture-item construction with per-class negatives.\\n- OWNERSHIP: `canonicaljson` keeps its `rejectUnsupportedImmutableObjectShape` rows (that table's census pins every row); this package is the validating owner and reuses `Canonicalize` (byte transform), `CalculateObjectIdentity` plus local claim comparisons (blobs; never the attesting `VerifyObjectIdentity` entry — only the test fixture calls it — per the provhost no-attestation bound), `sessadapter.DecodeTuple`, the `environ` scalar gate set via delegating wrappers, `scalar`, `hosttrust`, and `localstore.PutBlob`. No `internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings + re-pin); clause map in `internal/clonebundle/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n- EVIDENCE: package suite green (86.8% statements), 64 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, one raw log per plant with subprocess exit, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`); `TestInstallRawBlobIsIdempotent` + `TestInstallRawBlobRefusals` prove the localstore delegation (double install agrees; forged claim, short/long/tampered bytes refuse); durability itself is the landed localstore discipline (purity bound for this package: no second write path). README package section added with test commands and no capability claim.\\n- REV3 (rework of review RUN-260917-c05bc8): P1-a descriptor identity linked to the entry at build + evidence verification; P1-b AX number model + nested-duplicate refusal on extension values at build + decode; P2-f/P2-a environ gate adoption with the character string measure; P2-b/P2-c decode-side negatives for every surviving row + verifier/install negatives with per-plant logs; P2-d duplicate raw keys refused; P2-e identity re-decode before hashing; P3-b content XOR enforced; P3-c one-per-plan-candidate refused at build; P3-a sanitizer hardened with the exact bound stated; P3-d/P3-e harness rows fixed; P3-f/g/h hygiene. Finding-by-finding table in `TASK-260830-24z2b3_results.md`.\\n- REV4 (rework of review RUN-260917-62d051; base refreshed 888ae3d→2fc6d50, authority now SPEC.v0.7.0 with byte-identical pinned sections): P1-c payload value model enforced for every event kind at build + decode with exact-int64 sealing (sealed bytes never round/collapse); P2-α